xnu 0212: a console a verbose boot can keep up with

The panel console painted every pixel of every glyph cell (a full row of
background stores per character) in write-combining Device memory, and cleared
the row it was about to use: for a 60-character line that is ~35k stores, and
the boot log outruns it, so the console lags seconds behind and a photo shows
where it was, not where it is.

Paint only the pixels each glyph sets, as one 64-bit store per pair, skip blank
font rows, and drop the per-row clear: a written row was cleared once by the
screen clear or filled with history by the last scroll, and the scroll clears
the half it is about to write. A shorter line over a longer one leans on that
contract, and it is the only one.
--- a/osfmk/arm64/mondrian_early.c
+++ b/osfmk/arm64/mondrian_early.c
@@ -124,9 +124,15 @@
 	}
 	if (c == '\n' || early_col == EARLY_COLS) {
 		early_col = 0;
+		/*
+		 * The row about to be written was cleared when the screen was
+		 * cleared, when the last scroll filled it with history, or by the
+		 * scroll that put history above the cursor: no extra clear per
+		 * line. CAREFUL: a shorter line over a longer one would depend on
+		 * it, so the invariant is the contract.
+		 */
 		if (early_row + 1 < EARLY_HUD_ROW0) {
 			early_row++;
-			mondrian_early_clear_row();
 		} else {
 			mondrian_early_scroll();
 		}
@@ -134,16 +140,30 @@
 			return;
 		}
 	}
+	/*
+	 * Only the pixels the glyph sets, one 64-bit store per pair of
+	 * neighbouring pixels: the framebuffer is write-combining Device-like
+	 * memory and a line's stores are what a verbose boot spends on the
+	 * console. The cell is background by contract, and a blank row of the
+	 * font paints nothing at all.
+	 */
+	_Static_assert(EARLY_SCALE == 2, "the pack below assumes scale 2");
 	const unsigned char *glyph = iso_font + (unsigned char)c * 16;
 	for (unsigned int gy = 0; gy < 16; gy++) {
+		unsigned char bits = glyph[gy];
+
+		if (bits == 0) {
+			continue;
+		}
 		for (unsigned int sy = 0; sy < EARLY_SCALE; sy++) {
-			volatile uint32_t *line = EARLY_FB +
+			volatile uint64_t *line = (volatile uint64_t *)(EARLY_FB +
 			    (early_row * EARLY_CELL_H + gy * EARLY_SCALE + sy) * EARLY_STRIDE +
-			    early_col * EARLY_CELL_W;
+			    early_col * EARLY_CELL_W);
+
 			for (unsigned int gx = 0; gx < 8; gx++) {
-				uint32_t pixel = (glyph[gy] & (1u << gx)) ? 0xffffffffu : 0xff000000u;
-				for (unsigned int sx = 0; sx < EARLY_SCALE; sx++) {
-					line[gx * EARLY_SCALE + sx] = pixel;
+				if (bits & (1u << gx)) {
+					/* pixels gx*2..gx*2+1 are the same u64 */
+					line[gx] = 0xffffffffffffffffull;
 				}
 			}
 		}
